; calldata_hole_is_in_range: a slot the host left unset still occupies its
; place in the calldata, so the slots after it keep their indices.
;
; spec/xqvm/ISA.md's INPUT row bounds the slot against the count the host
; fixed, and the entries of that sequence need not all be set. The VM
; holds an unset entry as RegVal::Unset and counts it in calldata.len().
; A host that dropped the unset entry would turn [null, 5] into a single
; slot, so reading slot 1 would raise CallDataIndex instead of returning 5.

PUSH 1
INPUT r0         ; slot 1 is populated, and the hole at 0 does not shift it
PUSH 0
OUTPUT r0
HALT
